Need vs want.  If you are burdened you are carrying enough
that you risk death.  Prioritize and drop some items.  Nethack
is a game of judgement call after judgement call.  Now is the
time to start making judgements.  Exactly which item do you
think is least likely to be needed soon?  Drop that item in
your hoard in this level.  Lather rinse repeat.

> I've heard that you shouldn't become burdened as much as
> possible in one of the guides I've read. I need to identify my
> inventory quick. What's the fastest way to do this? I don't have any
> identify scrolls on me.

For efficiency price ID may be best.  It does not consume
any charges from wands, etc, but it is ambiguous for some
items.

> I've found many gems so far and just have two questions about them.
If
> your inventory splits the same type of gems into two slots in your
> inventory does that always mean that one of those slots are real gems
> while the others are fake? Also when dropping them on to an altar it
> always gives an uncursed status to them. Is it even possible to get
> cursed or blessed gems? If so, why do they uncursed status to them?

Gems have color, hardness and value.  Every single color has one
type of worthless glass that is soft.  Every hard gem is valuable
no matter its color.  Engrave in the floor and it's hard, engrave
in the dust and it's soft.  Knowing hard gems are all valuable
only gets you part of the way there.

I #name gems like "red hard 1" or "white soft 1" after I have
engraved with them.  I may end up with numbers as high as "white
soft 3".  When I have more than one of each specific soft type, I
throw one at a co-aligned unicorn.  Unicorns will drop glass, so
if the gem is droped then I pick it up and remain it "yellow
glass".  From then on I know all other yellow types are valuable.
If the unicorn keeps it I rename my remaining one "yellow value 3"
and I then know that is a valuable type.  At some point you will
discover every color of glass and you will know all other gems
are valuable.  I don't know if this works for the gray stones.

After that, price ID in a shop will tell you exactly which is
which.  Remember that at some point in the late game, identify
scrolls and spells will be so common you will have plenty to
spare on gems.  In the midgame once you know all of the glass
colors that's all you really need.

Glass is good for polymorph or for throwing as a weapon.  As
soon as you know one color of glass, all glass of that color
becomes ammunition.


